     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>You want the percentile rank of 1513.</p>\n<p>Open a copy of the file in Google Sheets. You cannot edit the original file.</p>\n<p>Look for the AvgSAT tab.</p>\n<p>Look for the Average SAT Score column.</p>\n<p>In a blank cell, enter the function: =PERCENTRANK(</p>\n<p>Click on the letter at the top of the Average SAT Score column.</p>\n<p>Then enter a comma, 1513, and close the parentheses: ,1513)</p>\n<p>The complete function probably looks like this: =PERCENTRANK(C:C,1513).</p>\n<p>You see the decimal value 0.992.</p>\n<p>Convert this to a percentage to say that this is the 99.2<sup>nd</sup> percentile.</p>"
    },
